{{- /*
    lookupPath — lookup a machine-specific *relative* path and join it onto a
    base directory.

    Wraps `lookup` for the common case where the table holds paths. The tables
    themselves live in .chezmoidata/lookups.toml, which is plain TOML and so
    cannot call joinPath; this is where the join happens instead.

    Arguments (a dict):
      chezmoi  the caller's .chezmoi variable, passed through to lookup
      table    dict of key -> path relative to `base`
      base     directory the matched value is joined onto
      default  optional: relative path used when no key matches

    Returns "" when the lookup misses OR when `base` is itself empty — never a
    bare `base`, and never a bare relative path. Both would be silently wrong
    directories that exist, so callers can keep testing the result for
    emptiness to mean "not configured for this machine".

    Usage:
      {{ includeTemplate "lookupPath" (dict
           "chezmoi" .chezmoi
           "base"    .chezmoi.homeDir
           "table"   .lookups.vscodeUserDir.table) }}
*/ -}}
{{- $rel := includeTemplate "lookup" (dict
      "chezmoi" .chezmoi
      "table"   .table
      "default" (index . "default" | default "")) -}}
{{- if and $rel .base -}}
{{-   joinPath .base $rel -}}
{{- end -}}
